# Resolution
Fixed in `6443410` (`Recover partial object version reservations`).

The fix keeps `ReserveObjectVersion` command-owned but makes recovery from a
lost in-memory pending reservation monotonic. New reservations now choose the
maximum next-version candidate across the object-PG acting set instead of only
the current primary. Replica apply still rejects a command below the replica's
local counter, but lower replicas are allowed to advance forward under the
command. This may leave gaps in opaque version IDs after partial apply plus
restart, but it prevents divergent counters from making a versioning-enabled key
persistently unwritable.

Regression coverage added:

- `reserve_object_version_partial_apply_after_reopen_uses_max_counter`
  reproduces partial `ReserveObjectVersion` apply, drops the in-memory pending
  command through local-cluster reopen, then proves later reservations converge
  all acting replicas and continue to advance.
- `reserve_object_version_command_advances_lower_counter_forward` proves a
  replica with a lower local counter accepts and advances to a higher
  command-owned reservation.

Verification before the fix commit:

- `cargo nextest run -p storage reserve_object_version -- --nocapture`
- `cargo check -p storage -p server-core`
